nonobots wrote:

> For a while I tried the pure protection rakcet, but being so feeble and
> trying to get to minetown result in a *lot* of dead characters. Spiked
> pits, starvation, exploding chests, volley of arrows, etc. I think the
> strategy is good for VERY careful players and pros.
> 

If you are going to try the protection racket, be prepared to abandon the 
idea when it isn't practical. So if the top levels of the mines are dark 
bones files, give up (the temptation is to try to descend by digging a 
hole, but that can leave you on or below minetown at XL1 without a pet, and 
that is not good). Likewise if your pet dies or disappears you should 
probably give up on the racket for that game.

Starvation shouldn't be an issue: you are trying to get to minetown as fast 
as possible (once you have gathered sufficient gold). Exploding chests 
aren't a problem either: leave the chests until you get back from minetown. 
To avoid the pits and arrow traps, try never to step anywhere your pet 
hasn't been first.

If you have any potions of healing, use them to increase your hitpoints. 
Also, if you need to pray because your hitpoints are low then you should 
get an additional HP boost at the same time.

